{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>This city is near.</b> Its settlement is recent — it was settled only recently; therefore its measure has not yet been filled (Shabbat 10). And what is its nearness? From the generation of the division, when the people were divided and each began to settle in his place — and that was in the year of Peleg's death — and from there to here is 52 years, for Peleg died in year 48 of Abraham. How so? Peleg lived after begetting Reu 209 years; subtract from them 32 for when Serug was born, and from Serug until Nachor was born 30 — that is 62; and from Nachor until Terach was born 29 — that is 91; and from there until Abraham was born 70 — that is 161; give them 48 — that is 209. And that year was the year of the division. And when Sodom was destroyed Abraham was 99 years old — behold, from the generation of the division until here is 52 years. And Zoar delayed its settlement one year after the settlement of Sodom and its allies — as it says אִמָּלְטָה נָא — נָא in gematria is 51." "<b>Is it not a little one?</b> And are not its sins few, and You are able to spare it?" "<b>And my soul shall live</b> — in it. This is its midrash. And the plain sense of Scripture: it is but a small city and the people in it are few — you need not be troubled if You spare it, and my soul shall live in it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:32.189200120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}